## [1.1.6] - 2026-05-25 [EXPORT-PATH-SYNC]
- **EXPORT PATH REPAIR**:
  - Fixed the output folder selector so it stores the real selected folder path instead of only the folder name.
  - Added an export status line under the export button so the interface shows where the textures were written.
- **TEXTURE CREATION REPAIR**:
  - Added missing texture-source loading for Telescope, Arrow, Potion, Map, Book, Nether Wart, Blaze Powder, and Ghast Tear.
  - Export now creates a fallback texture source instead of silently skipping a selected texture.
- **MINECRAFT/KUBEJS PATH SYNC**:
  - Preserved the existing legacy `textures/items` and `textures/blocks` output.
  - Added standard Minecraft `assets/minecraft/textures/item` and `assets/minecraft/textures/block` mirrors.
  - Added KubeJS `kubejs/assets/kubejs/textures/item` and `kubejs/assets/kubejs/textures/block` mirrors.
  - Rebuilt the existing KubeJS startup script on export to prevent duplicate registry entries from breaking startup.
- **VERSION STEPPING**:
  - Incremented version to 1.1.6 [EXPORT-PATH-SYNC] across window titles, UI components, and export logs.

## [1.1.5] - 2026-05-25 [RESOLUTE-EXPORT]
- **CRISP 16x16 TEXTURE SCALING**:
  - Implemented high-fidelity Nearest-Neighbor scaling for all exported textures.
  - Ensures exported PNG files are guaranteed to be exactly 16x16 pixels.
- **EXPORT ENGINE COMPLETE CHECK**:
  - Integrated all selectable items from the registry tab into the export pipeline (including Helmet, Chestplate, Leggings, Boots, Armor, Fishing Rod, Spyglass, Amethyst Cluster, Honeycomb, Sugar, Bone, and Bundle).
  - Remapped blocks and clusters to correctly save under the `textures/blocks` directory.
- **VOID STORM SHADER VISUAL**:
  - Added **Void Storm** visualizer shader featuring a dynamic swirling dark purple/magenta radial storm background and pulsing purple ring overlays on active foreground pixels.
- **VERSION STEPPING**:
  - Incremented version to 1.1.5 [RESOLUTE-EXPORT] across window titles, UI components, and logs.

## [1.1.4] - 2026-05-25 [NAMING-EXPORT]
- **MATERIAL-BASED ASSET NAMING**:
  - Remapped the exported file names for material-dependent items, blocks, and tools.
  - **Ore Drop** is now saved as `<material>.png` (e.g. `Glitch Diamond.png` or `echo_stone.png`) so it creates the correct material item.
  - **Raw Ore** is saved as `raw_<material>.png`.
  - **Tools & Armor** are prepended with the material prefix, saving as `<material>_sword.png`, `<material>_pickaxe.png`, etc., as expected by Minecraft resource packs.
- **VERSION STEPPING**:
  - Incremented version to 1.1.4 [NAMING-EXPORT] across frames and configurations.

## [1.1.3] - 2026-05-25 [SHADER-EXPORT]
- **SHADER-TO-EXPORT CONNECTION**:
  - Connected the visualizer shaders (Vortex Bloom, Spectral Pulse, Aurora Wave, Cosmic Stardust, Matrix Rain, Holo Scanlines, and Neon Flicker) directly to the exported PNG texture files.
  - Transparent backgrounds (`a == 0`) now automatically render visual backgrounds matching the active shader when exported.
  - Active foreground shaders are directly baked as pixel filters on the items, blocks, and tools.
- **VERSION STEPPING**:
  - Incremented version to 1.1.3 [SHADER-EXPORT] across window titles, UI components, and logs.

